    "result_text": "The change is complete and the full test suite is green (278 tests, 0 failures).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the daily owner-registration cap in the owner creation endpoint.\n\n**`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** (`addOwner`):\n- Added a guard that returns **400 Bad Request** when 20 owners already carry today's registration date. The check runs right after the registration date is defaulted (so it reflects today's `LocalDate.now()`).\n- Added a helper `isDailyRegistrationLimitReached()` that counts existing owners whose `registrationDate` equals today and returns `true` at 20 or more.\n\n**`OwnerRestControllerV1Tests.java`**:\n- Added `createOwnerDailyRegistrationLimitReached`, which seeds 20 owners with today's registration date and asserts the 21st POST is rejected with 400.\n\nOnly V1 creates owners (V2 is read-only paging), so no other endpoint needed the change.",
